Wait, let me check that. Suppose z = a + bi. Then $\overline{z}$ = a - bi. The modulus of z is sqrt(a² + b²) and the modulus of $\overline{z}$ is also sqrt(a² + b²). Yep, same value. So |$\overline{z}$| = |z| = 5. 

Now, the question is about the modulus of $\overline{z}$ squared. So |\overline{z}^2|. I need to figure out what that is. Let me think about properties of modulus. 

